* What does F$STrap do with an init table that has no terminator?
*
* OS9_F_STrap walks the table with
*     while ((venc = os9_get_w(itab)) != $FFFF) { ... itab += 2; }
* and validates the pointer with IN_ARENA exactly ONCE, before the loop. Nothing
* re-checks it as itab advances, so the only thing that stops the walk is
* finding $FFFF somewhere in guest memory. The 68k arena is calloc'd, so an
* unterminated table reads zeros -- never $FFFF -- and the walk runs to the end
* of the arena and straight off it, reading host heap past emul_end.
*
* A guest is allowed to pass a bad table; it must get an error, not walk the
* emulator off its own arena.
*
* This program points a1 at four zero words with no $FFFF after them. Nothing
* else in the program supplies one, and everything beyond is zeroed arena.
*   - fixed:  F$STrap returns an error (carry set) -> "OK refused"
*   - broken: os9exec walks ~32MB and reads past the arena. Under ASan that is
*     a heap-buffer-overflow abort; without it, a silent out-of-bounds read.
*
* a0 = 0 is legal (means "use the current stack"), so only a1 is under test.
*
Prgrm     set 1
Objct     set 1
ReEnt     set $80
Type_Lang set (Prgrm<<8)+Objct
Attr_Rev  set (ReEnt<<8)+1
*
IWrite    set $8A
FSTrap    set $0E
FExit     set $06
*
 psect strapun,Type_Lang,Attr_Rev,0,800,start
*
start
 lea     table(pc),a1          a1 = table with NO $FFFF terminator
 moveq   #0,d0
 move.l  #0,a0                 a0 = 0: use the current stack (legal)
 trap    #0
 dc.w    FSTrap
 bcs     refused               carry set = error returned, which is correct
*
 lea     mbad(pc),a0
 move.l  #mbadlen,d1
 bsr     say
 bra     done
refused
 lea     mok(pc),a0
 move.l  #moklen,d1
 bsr     say
done
 moveq   #0,d1
 trap    #0
 dc.w    FExit
*
* say: a0 = text, d1 = length -- writes to stderr (path 2)
say
 move.w  #2,d0
 trap    #0
 dc.w    IWrite
 rts
*
* Four zero words and no terminator. Zero is a valid-looking vector offset, so
* the loop keeps going rather than stopping on something malformed.
table   dc.w 0,0,0,0
mok     dc.b "strapun: OK   refused an unterminated table",13
moklen  equ *-mok
mbad    dc.b "strapun: HUH  accepted an unterminated table",13
mbadlen equ *-mbad
*
 ends
